Revision history for Net-Async-Zitadel

{{$NEXT}}
    - Security: `verify_token_f` enforces its signature algorithm allow-list. A
      token signed with an algorithm outside the list (default RS256, RS384,
      RS512) is rejected even when its key is in the JWKS; widen the list for
      an instance that signs with PS*, ES* or EdDSA.
    - `verify_token_f` takes the allow-list as `accepted_alg` (name, arrayref or
      Regexp, as in Crypt::JWT); `accepted_key_alg` stays as an alias.
    - Split Net::Async::Zitadel::Error into one package per file
      (Error/Validation.pm, Error/Network.pm, Error/API.pm); the base module
      still loads all three, so `use Net::Async::Zitadel::Error` is unchanged
      for callers. Mirrors the WWW::Zitadel split; clears the dzil "provide map
      entries did not map to .pm files" warning.
    - Management API gains 28 `_f` methods, mirroring WWW::Zitadel 0.002 (same
      paths and payloads, Future return values, required arguments validated
      before any request):
      - user grants: update_user_grant_f, deactivate_user_grant_f,
        reactivate_user_grant_f, delete_user_grant_f
      - typed identity providers: create_jwt_idp_f, create_google_idp_f,
        create_azuread_idp_f, create_github_idp_f,
        create_github_enterprise_idp_f, create_gitlab_idp_f,
        create_gitlab_self_hosted_idp_f, create_apple_idp_f (private_key sent
        base64-encoded), create_ldap_idp_f (root_ca sent base64-encoded)
      - project roles: update_project_role_f, remove_project_role_f
      - applications: create_saml_app_f (metadata_xml sent base64-encoded, or
        metadata_url), update_saml_app_f, create_api_app_f
      - organization domains: add_org_domain_f,
        generate_org_domain_validation_f, validate_org_domain_f,
        set_primary_org_domain_f, list_org_domains_f, remove_org_domain_f
      - users and organizations: lock_user_f, unlock_user_f,
        resend_email_verification_f, reactivate_org_f
    - MIME::Base64 is now declared as a runtime dependency.
    - `jwks_f` survives a cancelled caller: every caller gets its own Future
      derived from the shared fetch, so cancelling one no longer leaves a
      cancelled Future in the in-flight slot for all later calls. Concurrent
      `force_refresh` calls now share one request as well.

0.001     2026-03-14 05:01:52Z

  - Initial release
  - Async OIDC client (Net::Async::Zitadel::OIDC):
    - discovery_f, jwks_f, verify_token_f, userinfo_f, introspect_f
    - token_f, client_credentials_token_f, refresh_token_f,
      exchange_authorization_code_f
    - TTL-based caching: discovery_ttl (default 3600s), jwks_ttl (default 300s)
    - JWKS in-flight coalescing: concurrent refresh requests share one Future
    - Automatic JWKS refresh retry on token verification failure (key rotation)
  - Async Management API client (Net::Async::Zitadel::Management):
    - Human users: list_users_f, get_user_f, create_human_user_f, update_user_f,
      deactivate_user_f, reactivate_user_f, delete_user_f
    - Passwords: set_password_f, request_password_reset_f
    - User metadata: set_user_metadata_f, get_user_metadata_f, list_user_metadata_f
    - Service users: create_service_user_f, list_service_users_f,
      get_service_user_f, delete_service_user_f
    - Machine keys: add_machine_key_f, list_machine_keys_f, remove_machine_key_f
    - Projects: list_projects_f, get_project_f, create_project_f,
      update_project_f, delete_project_f
    - Apps: list_apps_f, get_app_f, create_oidc_app_f, update_oidc_app_f,
      delete_app_f
    - Orgs: get_org_f, create_org_f, list_orgs_f, update_org_f, deactivate_org_f
    - Roles: add_project_role_f, list_project_roles_f
    - Grants: create_user_grant_f, list_user_grants_f
    - Identity Providers: create_oidc_idp_f, list_idps_f, get_idp_f,
      update_idp_f, delete_idp_f, activate_idp_f, deactivate_idp_f
  - Structured exception hierarchy (Net::Async::Zitadel::Error):
    - ::Validation, ::Network, ::API (with http_status, api_message)
  - Full BUILD validation for empty issuer/base_url
  - Examples: examples/verify_token.pl, client_credentials.pl, manage_users.pl
  - Integration test skeleton: t/10-integration.t (skipped without ZITADEL_ISSUER)
